# Only used if the web app is ever hosted as a static site (Netlify, Cloudflare
# Pages). The recommended setup serves it from the API process instead
# (SERVE_CLIENT=true) — see docs/08-DEPLOYMENT.md — and this file is ignored.
#
# Do NOT add an `/api/* https://your-api... 200` proxy line and expect it to
# work on Cloudflare Pages: Pages only proxies relative paths on the same site,
# never an external domain. Without a same-origin API the refresh cookie is
# dropped and users are logged out on every reload.

# Single-page-app fallback: serve index.html for any path so that refreshing
# on /reports/board does not 404 on a static host.
/*      /index.html                               200
